1
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,680
With supplies being limited,

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,941
we'll need to add a rule allowing
passage in and out of the colony.

3
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:14,220
But I can't afford to let players like
Dhruv, who attack people indiscriminately,

4
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:15,720
leave the barriers.

5
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,457
I should wait until the players like him

6
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:21,187
are eliminated from the
other colonies first.

7
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,992
Communication between colonies is a must.

8
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,497
There's the two rules Fushiguro proposed,

9
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:29,437
a means of communication and
passage in and out of the colonies.

10
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:33,696
So we'll need four additional rules
to get the situation under control?

11
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,900
Everyone's still at their physical
and emotional limit from Shibuya.

12
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:42,780
Gojo, I won't let you kill
your best friend twice!

13
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,540
I'll kill Kenjaku myself.

14
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:49,460
I'll get the 400 points on my own

15
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,524
Okay, you can all come out now.

16
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:02,657
I think we should continue making our
way north to the edge of the barrier.

17
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:03,880
Can you carry me?

18
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:06,164
Just hang in there, sweetheart.

19
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,137
Why don't we take a quick rest?

20
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:09,161
We're safe here.

21
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:12,557
This stadium was being controlled
by the sorcerer I just defeated.

22
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:15,937
Any player that comes along
will be pretty hesitant to...

23
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:17,079
What's that sound?

24
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:24,000
Quick, get into the stadium. Let's go!

25
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:25,810
Let's get out of here!

26
00:01:25,893 --> 00:01:26,723
Hurry up.

27
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:27,770
No!

28
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:32,500
No! No!

29
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:34,500
No! No!

30
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:35,890
No!

31
00:01:35,973 --> 00:01:36,803
No!

32
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:42,330
No!

33
00:01:42,413 --> 00:01:43,648
Are these cockroaches real?

34
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,360
Rika, knock it down! Hurry!

35
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:13,060
Kogane, is that a player?

36
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:16,540
Yes, that is a player called Kuro Arushi.

37
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:20,500
So some players are cursed spirits.

38
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,980
I'm being watched.

39
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:52,397
Likely, it's the other two
players with high points.

40
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,940
Why do you interfere?

41
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,440
Kuro Urushi is a cursed spirit.

42
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:59,660
Why do you kill us?

43
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,960
I can exercise it.

44
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:07,062
I just have to drive positive energy from
my reverse curse technique into its body.

45
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:10,480
I can ask you the same question, but...

46
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:14,300
Because I like the taste of Naira!

47
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:22,367
I don't want those other two players to
know I can use reverse curse technique.

48
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:25,009
Rika is protecting
everyone in the stadium,

49
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:30,062
so I have to exercise Kuro Urushi without
using Rika or my reverse curse technique.

50
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,560
Blinding! Blinding! Blinding!

51
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,240
Hmph!

52
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:30,600
Ah!

53
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,837
Ah! Ah!

54
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:35,640
Uh... Ah! Uh...

55
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:38,277
Uh...

56
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:41,160
Ah! Ah! Amai!

57
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:54,017
You have gained five points for a kill.

58
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,080
I see that you can use.

59
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,620
Reverse Cursed Technique.

60
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:08,420
What was that? A strike?

61
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,597
My arm is back to normal.

62
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,977
I feel fine.

63
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:24,457
Her technique probably manipulates space.

64
00:05:24,540 --> 00:05:27,897
But I guess she can't use that
space to crush her opponents.

65
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:31,180
It seems to create distortions
like a funhouse mirror.

66
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,557
You're wondering about my technique.

67
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:36,360
It treats the sky as a surface.

68
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,677
Here let me show you.

69
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,737
She's revealing her technique.

70
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:44,317
Hurry up and attack already.

71
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,417
I have to ask.

72
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:49,357
You're not someone who's going to
complain about getting killed, are you?

73
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:53,237
I mean I can understand powerless
people getting desperate for points.

74
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:56,597
But a strong person like you can
claim points whenever they want.

75
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:59,957
So what's your reason for
actively seeking a fight?

76
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:03,737
This little brat seriously are you?

77
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:06,157
Modern day sorcerers that
casual about incarnation?

78
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,177
To us from the old school.

79
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,997
This means coming back from the dead.

80
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:14,897
People who lived out their lives without
regrets wouldn't accept Kenjaku's offer,

81
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:15,810
would they?

82
00:06:15,893 --> 00:06:17,857
He's really pissing me off.

83
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:19,897
I like to think of the culling game as the

84
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:22,257
first step toward a
chance at a second life.

85
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:25,737
Keep in mind that Kenjaku
set the stage for this.

86
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,157
Anything could happen.

87
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:28,070
We need to?

88
00:06:28,153 --> 00:06:30,037
to earn points to prepare ourselves.

89
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:33,355
I wonder if someone like you
has any friends or lovers.

90
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:35,730
Huh?

91
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,660
You know what?

92
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:40,117
Until recently, I didn't
have any friends either.

93
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:41,965
Not that I feel sorry for you.

94
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:46,240
This feeling, it's like he's
hunting for things that trigger me.

95
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:49,757
Your pain was caused
thousands of years ago.

96
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:52,597
The people alive today have
nothing to do with your regrets.

97
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:55,337
How many have to die until
you finally feel avenged?

98
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:57,440
Wait just a minute.

99
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,820
Are you one of the Fujiwara?

100
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:03,800
How can anyone from your
bloodline understand me?

101
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,780
Granite blast.

102
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:26,710
Ishigori?

103
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:28,580
It came from that rooftop.

104
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:30,400
Too close for comfort.

105
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:35,557
Even with Rika protecting the stadium, a
direct hit from an attack on that level?

106
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:37,480
will leave several people dead.

107
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:40,140
So I have to take Ishigori out first.

108
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:45,420
Now that Code Urushi and Dhruv are gone,
I have no reason to let Ishigori run free.

109
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,880
I'll take both him and Okotsu out.

110
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:51,940
Brennan Blast!

111
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:07,820
Come on, don't disappoint me.

112
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,960
He's gone.

113
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:13,980
No, that's where Akotsu
dug a hole earlier.

114
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:21,717
Can't you fight without blowing
up everything around you?

115
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:25,640
Oh, but that won't
satisfy my hunger, Okotsu.

116
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:32,757
Would you tell a starving
kid with a feast in

117
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:35,880
front of him to take
his time and eat slower?

118
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,460
Wouldn't anyone?

119
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:41,180
I guess so.

120
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:42,576
Most probably would.

121
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:44,053
That was a bad example.

122
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:48,580
My first run at life was in
completely lacking flavor.

123
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:52,080
Some of the guys I
fought had real backbone.

124
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:54,360
I even met a nice woman, too.

125
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:58,356
Frankly, it'd be hard to say
I had any regrets at all.

126
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:05,920
This vague hunger I constantly feel
is always gnawing at me, Okotsu.

127
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:09,872
Everyone's always wondering
what I'm so unsatisfied about.

128
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:15,160
These cigarettes have a
slightly sweet aftertaste.

129
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:18,080
You know what it was?

130
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:20,780
There was no dessert in my life.

131
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,080
Here it comes!

132
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:35,800
Why am I unsatisfied I think you know?

133
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:47,060
I'm unsatisfied because I'm not fulfilled.

134
00:10:00,780 --> 00:10:02,820
You better not be crushed.

135
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:21,180
Hey, what's the hair?

136
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:39,410
Nice!

137
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,720
Not calling you a Shikigami?

138
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:50,800
I can't right now.

139
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:53,120
Not with you going wild.

140
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:55,260
Oh, that's a shame.

141
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:01,207
He's probably trying to
limit where I can go.

142
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,180
But I'll break through.

143
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,420
Head on!

144
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:08,050
Sweet!

145
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,280
That's it, Akutsu!

146
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:11,740
Keep on coming!

147
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:15,637
This cursed energy!

148
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,550
So precise!

149
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:23,858
Here's your reward.

150
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:30,230
Uh-oh.

151
00:11:30,313 --> 00:11:32,020
I overheated my hand.

152
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,360
You're good, Oko-choo.

153
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:44,260
Could you be the one?

154
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:46,180
Are you my dessert?

155
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:54,320
You're great!

156
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:56,560
Best I've seen so far!

157
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:05,340
What I strike isn't the person,
but the surface of the sky.

158
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,580
Thin icebreaker!

159
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:14,440
Get lost, you pile of vomit!

160
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:20,520
Shut your mouth, dick cheese!

161
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:27,820
This guy's resilient.

162
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,500
Glad you're alive.

163
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:31,940
I wanted to torment you some more.

164
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:34,560
What a hit.

165
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:38,684
That was the first time I've been
forced to eat my old technique.

166
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,517
Reverse Cursed Technique
is a pain to deal with,

167
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,860
but it burns Cursed Energy like crazy.

168
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:49,860
We're finally seeing the bottom
of your reserves, Okotsu.

169
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:52,532
No matter how high end the sweet shop is,

170
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:56,980
seeing the displays empty at closing
time is always disappointing.

171
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,440
Guess it wasn't you.

172
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:08,857
I wanted to gain more distance
from everyone in the stadium.

173
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:10,517
Keep them out of harm's way.

174
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,520
Oh well.

175
00:13:16,180 --> 00:13:18,040
Come to me, Rika.

176
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,360
Give me everything!

177
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:25,540
Has Shikigami completely manifested?

178
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,118
How does that work?

179
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:29,715
Any swelling with cursed energy again?

180
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,960
Which would you like, Rika?

181
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:34,960
Thank you.

182
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,560
I'll take that one.

183
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:41,437
Rika is the stockpile of Cursed Energy and

184
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,577
the externalization of Okotsu's technique.

185
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:46,760
It remained with him after
Rika Orimoto passed on.

186
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:50,837
While connected to Rika through
the ring, he gains the following.

187
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:52,680
Use of his Cursed Technique,

188
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:57,292
the complete manifestation of Rika,
and the Cursed Energy supplied by Rika.

189
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:01,760
Yuta can remain connected
to Rika for five minutes.

190
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,460
Okay, let's go.

191
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:09,440
Don't underestimate me.

192
00:14:13,760 --> 00:14:14,960
Don't move.

193
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,160
Snake eyes and fangs.

194
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:18,680
I can't move.

195
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:24,840
Oh, man.

196
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:27,220
You are super sweet, huh?

197
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:30,330
Rika.

198
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:32,060
Rage! Yeah!

199
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:34,500
Oh, no!

200
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,540
That was close.

201
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:45,180
You can't get rid of me that easy!

202
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:15,940
Help me! You!

203
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:18,160
You hurt Yaga!

204
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:30,500
What now?

205
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,580
Let's go!

206
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:38,780
Even with this, I can't fully block it.

207
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:43,400
Wanna go?

208
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:50,180
Uh!

209
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:09,050
Huh?

210
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:14,060
Finn, icebreaker!

211
00:16:33,060 --> 00:16:34,320
Fujiwara!

212
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:38,060
I've still got a strong appetite!

213
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:42,380
Let's keep chowing down!

214
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:46,140
It's always you, Fujiwara.

215
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:48,322
You're always getting in my way.

216
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:50,480
Are you that afraid of me?

217
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:52,918
Afraid of me becoming my own person?

218
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:01,557
Okotsu defeated Drew Vlaktawala,

219
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:06,420
whose technique made the path of
his Shikigami into his domain?

220
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:09,380
which cut into anything it touched.

221
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:15,500
This is Dhruv's technique.

222
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:20,940
Does that mean Bakotsu's
technique is copy?

223
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:38,257
I don't know what my ancestors did to
you, but that has nothing to do with me.

224
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:42,877
If you live only for your own sake, you're
eventually going to reach your limit.

225
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:43,790
Shut up.

226
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:45,560
Live for the sake of others?

227
00:17:45,860 --> 00:17:48,280
You think I'll eventually reach my limit?

228
00:17:49,780 --> 00:17:51,720
Stop barking those things at me!

229
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:55,315
It's easy for you to say
you've already become someone!

230
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,540
Quit your whining,

231
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:17,180
because at this point,
words are meaningless!

232
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:24,100
Don't leave expansion!

233
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:29,280
Future, give me back!

234
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,704
Even if it tries to
penetrate the barrier later!

235
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:36,547
I ain't gonna drag this out,
let's settle this nice and sweet!

236
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:42,837
At that moment, the black
devil of the modern age...

237
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:47,560
I told you, I like the taste of iron!

238
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:49,849
...flew into the barriers.

239
00:18:52,660 --> 00:18:57,080
Kurourushi had completed
Parthenogenesis before going dormant.

240
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:02,420
So Kurourushi was still alive
and well as a cursed spirit.

241
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:07,337
The complex forces of their domains had
been keeping the three sorcerers in check.

242
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:10,637
But this intruder was unexpected,

243
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:16,820
and so the barriers collapsed.

244
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:24,800
How's Kuro Orushi still alive?

245
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:33,580
Damn, I can't use my technique
right after domain expansion.

246
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:43,740
How dare you take my arm? Fujiwara!

247
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:46,200
Enough, Uro. Quiet.

248
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:50,480
You and the roach were
never invited to my table.

249
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:53,740
Granite blast.

250
00:19:57,680 --> 00:20:00,680
Ishigori's technique is
cursed energy discharge.

251
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:03,160
It's an extremely simple attack,

252
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:08,700
but it performs just as well, even
when his technique is burnt out.

253
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:19,040
Now...

254
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:25,940
Welcome to my table, Okotsu.

255
00:20:26,740 --> 00:20:28,800
Rika, let's go.

256
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:37,120
Okotsu can discharge a high
volume of Cursed Energy,

257
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:41,180
but only while Rika is
completely manifested. However,

258
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:45,380
his maximum output is slightly
inferior to Ishigori's,

259
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:48,297
so he planned to charge
and unleash his Cursed

260
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:51,700
Energy before Ishigori
reached maximum output.

261
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,940
But he changed his mind.

262
00:20:57,660 --> 00:20:59,937
400 years of longing.

263
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:03,457
